IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P4-gate`

-- P4-annex-vii: Annex VII, "Conformity based on an assessment of the quality management system and an assessment of the technical documentation" (consolidated lines 1800 to 1839).
-- The Omnibus did not change Annex VII (no passage of it carries a marker; the marker `▼B` before Annex VIII's text is not in it): one text, both versions.
-- Annex VII is given effect by Article 43 (Chapter III Section 5): its group is `General` (assumed, not ruled: PLAN.md section 3).
-- Every function takes the four inputs of the keel's applicability function (the date asked, the route to high-risk, the placement date, the changed flag)
-- and answers NOTHING where Annex VII does not apply to the AI system on the date asked (before 2 August 2026, a system that is not high-risk, or a system saved by Article 111(2)).
-- Every function also takes the two further inputs of the keel's Article 2(2) (the products are covered by the legislation of Section B of Annex I; the requirements have been integrated in it)
-- and answers JUST FALSE where Article 2(2) says that Article 43, and with it Annex VII, does not apply to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach: assumed, not ruled).
-- Article 43(3) applies only some points of Annex VII to the high-risk AI systems of Section A of Annex I; that is Article 43's (another part's): seam S-43, not encoded here.
-- A duty whose "where" or "if" is unmet answers NOTHING (fork F-unmet-where); a bare "shall" not done answers JUST FALSE (fork F-bare-shall).

§ `Annex VII: the parties and acts of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `Annex VII party` IS ONE OF
    `Annex VII provider`
    `Annex VII notified body`

DECLARE `Annex VII act` IS ONE OF
    `Annex VII 3.2 assess the quality management system and determine whether it satisfies the requirements referred to in Article 17`
    `Annex VII 3.2 notify the decision to the provider or its authorised representative`
    `Annex VII 3.3 continue to implement and maintain the approved quality management system`
    `Annex VII 3.4 bring the intended change to the attention of the notified body`
    `Annex VII 3.4 examine the proposed changes and decide whether a reassessment is necessary`
    `Annex VII 3.4 notify the provider of its decision on the changes`
    `Annex VII 4.1 lodge an application for the assessment of the technical documentation with a notified body of the provider's choice`
    `Annex VII 4.3 examine the technical documentation`
    `Annex VII 4.4 itself directly carry out adequate tests`
    `Annex VII 4.6 notify the decision to the provider or its authorised representative`
    `Annex VII 4.6 issue a Union technical documentation assessment certificate`
    `Annex VII 4.6 refuse to issue a Union technical documentation assessment certificate and inform the applicant accordingly, giving detailed reasons`
    `Annex VII 4.7 inform the notified body of the intended change or of the occurrence of such a change`
    `Annex VII 4.7 assess the changes and decide whether they require a new conformity assessment`
    `Annex VII 4.7 assess the changes, notify the provider of its decision and, where the changes are approved, issue a supplement`
    `Annex VII 5.2 allow the notified body to access the premises where the design, development and testing of the AI systems is taking place`
    `Annex VII 5.2 share with the notified body all necessary information`
    `Annex VII 5.3 carry out periodic audits and provide the provider with an audit report`

§ `Annex VII point 1: the procedure`

-- src:1803 | Conformity based on an assessment of the quality management system and an assessment of the technical documentation is the conformity assessment procedure based on points 2 to 5.
@ref Annex VII point 1 (src:1803)
-- Gloss: the procedure of Annex VII is the one whose three parts are the assessment of the quality management system (point 3), the assessment of the technical documentation (point 4) and the surveillance of the approved quality management system (point 5).
-- Whether Annex VII is the procedure that applies to a given system is Article 43's question (seam S-43); this function says what the procedure consists of.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the quality management system has been assessed in accordance with point 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation has been assessed in accordance with point 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approved quality management system is under surveillance in accordance with point 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex VII point 1 the conformity assessment is the procedure based on points 2 to 5` MEANS
    `Annex VII the answer when the group applies` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation`
        (   `the quality management system has been assessed in accordance with point 3`
        AND `the technical documentation has been assessed in accordance with point 4`
        AND `the approved quality management system is under surveillance in accordance with point 5`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is the conformity assessment procedure based on points 2 to 5" (a definition: a conformity assessment lacking any of the three parts is not the procedure)

§ `Annex VII point 2: overview`

-- src:1805 | The approved quality management system for the design, development and testing of AI systems pursuant to Article 17 shall be examined in accordance with point 3 and shall be subject to surveillance as specified in point 5. The technical documentation of the AI system shall be examined in accordance with point 4.
@ref Annex VII point 2 (src:1805)
-- Gloss: the quality management system the notified body approved is examined as point 3 says and watched over as point 5 says.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approved quality management system has been examined in accordance with point 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approved quality management system is subject to surveillance as specified in point 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex VII point 2 first sentence the approved quality management system has been examined and is under surveillance` MEANS
    `Annex VII the answer when the group applies` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation`
        (   `the approved quality management system has been examined in accordance with point 3`
        AND `the approved quality management system is subject to surveillance as specified in point 5`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be examined in accordance with point 3 and shall be subject to surveillance as specified in point 5" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- src:1805 | The approved quality management system for the design, development and testing of AI systems pursuant to Article 17 shall be examined in accordance with point 3 and shall be subject to surveillance as specified in point 5. The technical documentation of the AI system shall be examined in accordance with point 4.
@ref Annex VII point 2 (src:1805)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation of the AI system has been examined in accordance with point 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex VII point 2 second sentence the technical documentation has been examined` MEANS
    `Annex VII the answer when the group applies` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation`
        (`the technical documentation of the AI system has been examined in accordance with point 4`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The technical documentation of the AI system shall be examined in accordance with point 4" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Annex VII point 3.1: the application of the provider for the assessment of the quality management system`

